    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the September 7th slate with **Trea Turner** headlining the lineup as the clear anchor. With a score of 76.61, **Trea Turner** benefits from an optimal batting position and a favorable matchup against the right-handed Holmes, mitigating the standard platoon disadvantage to deliver elite utility. Complementing this, **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (69.31) provide the day's highest power-ceiling potential. **Kazuma Okamoto** is particularly well-positioned, as a 4.67 xERA from the opposing arm and a favorable park factor provide a +16% boost to his skill projection, while **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Cantillo, making both primary targets for our Roto output today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the bottom of the order and the bench. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.47) earns his spot despite a significant -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Gasser; his inclusion is driven entirely by our aggressive prioritization of stolen bases, as his matchup against Gasser\u2019s slow delivery adds a +4% efficiency premium that makes him a superior choice to **Dillon Dingler**. While **Dillon Dingler** (36.60) was the closest to cracking the lineup, his suboptimal ranking against Ryan\u2014compounded by a -15% platoon hit\u2014kept him safely below our 40-point threshold. Similarly, **Pedro Ramirez** remains a marginal play at 43.10; while he provides flexibility, his position at the bottom of the order suppresses his counting stat value. We remain mindful that **Christian Yelich** (52.41) carries risk, as his production against left-handed pitching is hampered by a significant platoon penalty, and he remains a candidate for early substitution if the game situation dictates protecting our weekly Roto caps.",
